# E3J9 curated credential PATH — /opt/eanhl-cloud/credential-bin (design §3).
#
# Non-secret. Each line is `<link name> <absolute target>`: the installed
# directory holds exactly one root-owned symlink per line, named <link name>
# and pointing at <absolute target>, and nothing else (acceptance check A1).
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Source basis: password-store.sh@1.7.4 (sha256 b48d710a…bcd7), split by path
# in design §3; unchanged for the accepted Ubuntu pass 1.7.4-8 (sha256
# b0da432e…8632), whose only differences are the hunks H1-H7 recorded in
# pass-1.7.4-8.accepted-delta.escaped. `cat` is required by pass's usage and
# error paths.
#
# The upstream platform `source` line is absent from the installed pass (H1),
# so `uname`, `cut` and `tr` are NOT needed and are never installed.
#
# Symlink chains (A1/A2): several targets are themselves symlinks on the host
# (uutils multicall coreutils; `rm` → gnurm; `gpg` may be an alternative). A1
# records, for every target, the final `readlink -f` path, its owning package
# (`dpkg -S`), and root ownership and non-writability of every hop. Any change
# between sessions is a STOP.
bash /usr/bin/bash
getopt /usr/bin/getopt
gpg /usr/bin/gpg
pass /usr/bin/pass
mkdir /usr/bin/mkdir
dirname /usr/bin/dirname
grep /usr/bin/grep
find /usr/bin/find
base64 /usr/bin/base64
rm /usr/bin/rm
rmdir /usr/bin/rmdir
cat /usr/bin/cat
#
# Never present: tty, xdg-open, any browser or opener, which, gpg2, git, tree,
# uname, cut, tr, or any command not derived from the source inventory above.
